title: Abandoned Ballroom
subtitle: Municipal survey
priority: 2
max-visits: 1
tags: event
new-page: true
view-if: month = 5 and year = 2303 and abandoned_ballroom = 0
on-arrival: abandoned_ballroom = 1

A maintainence team was shocked today to stumble upon a giant abandoned ballroom in the Docks district.  A search in the archives eventually determined that the ballroom dates back to the early days of Mikasa but was apparently never opened because of security concerns.  The site is absolutely massive and features an enormous amount of gold fixtures and gold plating.  Apparently around the time it was constructed gold was seen as a conspicious way to display wealth.  Ironically the asteroid mining rush drastically lowered the price of gold and it's prestige status about a decade after the construction.  Our archivest noted that when it was built the ballroom would have been seen as embarrassingly gaudy and once the price of gold crashed people would have found it hilarious... if they knew it existed.

Despite being located on the fringes of the Docks district, the site is already well integrated into the city infrastructure and represents prime real estate.  The corporations and local elites would love to get their hands on it.  But it also could be very easily converted into housing for refugees, ironically putting some of the poorest people in Mikasa into one of it's best locations.

- @refugee_housing: Convert the ballroom into refugee housing
- @give_brazos: Grant the site to Brazos Zaibatsu
- @give_magrail: Grant the site to Combined Magrail Trust
- @give_soylent: Grant the site to Community Soylent
- @local_elites: Reserve the site for Docks local elites

